Now I understand the layout. The issue is in the `calc-months-grid` ΓÇö a 3-column grid (2 on mobile) where each cell contains a range input with `flex: 1` but no `min-width: 0`. Range inputs have an intrinsic minimum width (~100-120px) that prevents them from shrinking below that, even with `flex: 1 1 0%`. This pushes the grid cells wider than the available container at 390px.

The fix: add `minWidth: 0` to the range input so it can shrink below its intrinsic minimum.

